      "id": "botchan-s03-p0008",
      "source_en": "Thus it was all right with the school, but it would not do with the home where I boarded. I could have borne pretty well with the landlord who came and helped himself to the tea from my own can, but he was not content with that. He would bring various things in and tried to make a customer of me. Some dozen ornamental seals were first brought in by him, who asked me to buy them for three yen and said it was a bargain. I told him that I, not being a poor artist going around country places, did not need them. Next time he came in with a hanging scroll of flowers and birds painted by a certain",
